        "observations": [
          "No concrete source blocker found. One appended focused test and helpers preserve the entire original 63,444-byte test file as an exact prefix: 242 baseline macros/nine tests remain, now 313 macros/ten tests. Production, Slint, models and reference inputs are unchanged.",
          "The actual Add Defaults Button is physically pressed/released at (1019,440) only after real rendering settles at 1100 × 800, scale 1, zero content scroll and no search/matches. A prior empty popup stack must become exactly one popup without creating another native adapter; no callback fallback or pointer retry is used. Escape restores zero popups with complete rows/flags, saved Manager and child slots unchanged.",
          "Physical popup Down/Return routes distinguish row 0 add-all from row 1 select-some by their actual results. The exact platform prompt and custom answer labels are compared against the Qt recording; all/everything adds the complete recorded sorted names/selection and selector/everything opens fifteen recorded ordered false choices. The actual menu text and ordering still need fresh image inspection.",
          "The selector initial/selected states compare all fifteen labels and booleans, then only indices 0/9. Parent saved Manager remains unchanged until Options Apply. Persisted typed OS defaults preserve all fields except fresh keys, which are unique and differ from every original factory key; the prior call is unchanged. Complete reopened row cells and unselected booleans match the saved Manager.",
          "The successor test retires a genuinely pending selector through parent Cancel, gives the new live selector an independently chosen row 1, then invokes old toggle/Apply/Cancel/native-close and old parent actions. Full current selector names/booleans, parent cells/flags, saved Manager, Options/default slot identity and window visibility remain unchanged. Positive current acceptance adds exactly xdg-open to the staged draft, followed by parent Cancel preserving Store.",
          "Current Cancel, native CloseRequested and supported slot cancellation each discard newly selected row 14 without changing parent rows or Store and without closing the parent. Automatic Main destruction, final Bound drop or arbitrary hidden/page-switch admission are not tested here.",
          "Captures retain actual owner adapters, advance real timers and render/animation state, require at least 35 ms and consecutive equal pixel buffers, and fail within two seconds. The reused helper asserts a visible window and never forces child flags or caption state.",
          "Current Slint1.18 popup/key APIs match existing pinned usages. Short-lived RefCell reads, private active-popup access, WindowEvent key/close dispatch and factory vector removal are compatible with the current sources. No immediate type/lint/borrow blocker was found, but compilation/runtime success is not inferred from source review."
        ],
        "finite_limits": [
          "Exactly audit-options-external-programs-external-calls-add-defaults. No Add/Edit/Delete/Duplicate/import/export, process/list/reopen parents, aliases, default-route launch integration or broader ownership credit follows.",
          "Physical opening and popup keyboard selection are bounded to the measured 1100 × 800, scale 1, unscrolled/no-search Options page. Default/universal geometry, OS menu placement or physical selector toggles/Apply buttons are not established; selector/platform answers use callbacks.",
          "Actual unchanged Qt default_routes and defaults_by_platform match without normalization. The recorder drives real handlers with scripted answers/selection. Its only PNG is a callable child, not a defaults popup/question/selector, so no paired Qt pixel, timing, dialog-decoration or placement parity is available.",
          "Native selector rows use highlighted TableRow.selected values rather than Qt checkbox widgets. Exact boolean/choice behavior does not establish checkbox pixel parity. All fifteen rows, footer and selected highlights plus the long custom platform labels must be readable in the fresh captures.",
          "Supported captures use 1100 × 800 parent/composite, 600 × 550 selector and 520 × 200 platform question. Long command columns may elide; full typed Store values are asserted independently. Geometry/font/framework differences must be retained after fresh review.",
          "The new persisted choice pair contains OS File/URL defaults; the all-default draft compares complete rendered row cells, while prior factory/model/serialized tests provide separate process/platform evidence. No new execution of defaults, every typed process rule or OS launcher is claimed.",
          "Retirement is scoped to parent Cancel against a live successor plus ordinary selector Cancel/native-close/slot cancellation. No automatic Main destruction, final Bound drop, temporary hide/page-switch or generic controller-lifetime guarantee is claimed.",
          "Exact final integrated source, full strict Linux CI and all six source-bound fresh images remain required. Windows and macOS are deferred. This source-only review grants no feature/status or runtime/render approval."
